 "note": "X_ITE 16.6.0: a CollisionSpace is only a list of collidables, flattened through nested spaces (and re-flattened live when a nested list changes). `enabled` and `useGeometry` are never read: CS2 holds the same two nested spaces switched off and with useGeometry true and reports exactly what CS1 reports (1 contact, intersections BS and GS). A space inside the world's own collider changes nothing in the physics; it matters only through a CollisionSensor.collider. Emptying SA at run time ends the contact of CS1 within a frame (isActive false) and leaves its stale contacts list.",
